Use case: logo-brand.
Asset type: extra-wide GitHub README hero banner for the FROST temporal graph neural network training framework.
Create a polished, understated, professional research-software banner. Extremely horizontal composition, target 3072 by 1024 pixels (3:1), full-bleed near-black/navy background matching GitHub dark mode, generous horizontal margins and calm negative space. Subtle thin ice-blue temporal graph edges and small nodes flow left-to-right behind the typography, with a few restrained parallel routing paths and synchronization connections. Background graphics should be delicate and low contrast, not a detailed scientific diagram; no fake labels or hardware logos.
The hero is primarily typography. The ONLY text in the image must be exactly:
"Forward-looking Routing and"
"Orchestrated Synchronization for TGNN"
These are two balanced, very large, crisp, readable typographic lines centered vertically and horizontally. Use a clean modern sans-serif, medium/bold weight. First line slightly shorter than second is fine, same font size throughout. Spell Orchestrated and Synchronization correctly.
IMPORTANT LETTER COLOR REQUIREMENT: highlight ONLY these FIVE initial letters in luminous ice cyan, slightly heavier weight: F in Forward-looking, R in Routing, O in Orchestrated, S in Synchronization, T in TGNN. All the rest of the letters, including "and", "for", and "GNN", must be soft off-white. These five emphasized letters spell F R O S T when read in order. Do not color entire words. Do not print markdown, brackets, underscores, quotation marks, or letter-selection marks. Keep normal word spacing and natural kerning.
Do not add a separate FROST title, subtitle, badges, watermark or any other text. Ensure all text is easily legible when the banner is displayed at roughly 900px wide. Use only subtle cyan illumination, no neon overload, no snow landscape, no mascots, no glossy 3D typography. Final image should look carefully typeset, minimal, elegant, and very wide.
